Dear Mori,
Thank you for the
note and interest in Pathview.
For KEGG view, we
map the user data onto native KEGG graph. And the resolution is really bounded
by the original KEGG graph. The argument res in the keggview.native function is
there to help the development process and will be removed eventually. It has
little effect if you want to achieve higher resolution. As you note that it may
change Pathview stamp font size (and gene label sizes when same.layer=F).
I would recommend you
sticking to the default resolution setting, which has been optimized over the
development process. The graphs in the Pathview papers and tutorials were all
generated using the default resolution setting. We can?t really do anything to improve
the original KEGG graph. However, improper conversion of the PNG image into PDF
format (for instance, in some journal editing process) may lower the
resolution. HTH.
Weijun





