Message-ID: <51D51DFA.6010503@upf.edu>

hi Paul, just in case it helps, the current definition of the 
edgeMatrix() method for 'graphBAM' is:

setMethod("edgeMatrix", "graphBAM",
           function (object, duplicates = FALSE) {
             bitvec <- object at edgeSet@bit_vector
             nds <- nodes(object)
             df <- .Call(graph_bitarray_rowColPos, bitvec)
             t(df)
           })

so clearly the argument 'duplicates' is not taken into account, i 
believe a possible fix could be the following:

setMethod("edgeMatrix", "graphBAM",
           function(object, duplicates=FALSE) {
             bitvec <- object at edgeSet@bit_vector
             nds <- nodes(object)
             df <- .Call(graph_bitarray_rowColPos, bitvec)
             if (duplicates)
               df <- rbind(df, cbind(as.vector(df[, "to"]),
                           as.vector(df[, "from"])))
             t(df)
           })


cheers,
robert.

