> array weights but not gene weights. Because the analysis of RNA-seq
> data requires also gene weights, then romer() would need to be
> modified to accept gene weights as well. Then voom() could be used
> directly. In
> camara()/roast() voom based analysis gene weights are used in order to
> estimate the mean-variance relationship from the data and
> array-weights are used to normalize between library sizes - this
> generates a weights matrix that is used in the analysis by limma
> functions including camera and roast.  Btw. voom(), camera() and
> roast() are still part of limma but just referred to in the edgeR
> manual (they can be used also with other packages).
