table ( tapply( res2$pvalue < 0.1, geneIDs(ExonCountSet), any ) )
# FALSE   TRUE 
# 1364    5802

By checking the histogram of raw p-values of exons (NOT genes), I find that it is monotonically increasing from 0 to 1, with relatively few counting bins falling into the bins from 0 to 0.2.

My question is: does this result make sense in terms of DE testing? Among 240,000 counting bins, only 14,000 are with p-value < 0.1. If I randomly sample, then there would be ~240,000*0.1 = 24,000 counting bins called DE, so the result is really conservative (I think the signal of treatment is pretty strong so the result is weird). Can I know if there is any explanation for this situation?

